<title>SINGAPORE: Transpac ups stake in Taiwan associate.</title>
<headline>Transpac ups stake in Taiwan associate.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transpac Industrial Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday it planned to subscribe to 15.38 million new shares in United Multi Media Inc (UMM), a company formed to acquire existing cable television operators in Taiwan.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that UMM planned to raise its share capital by issuing 100 million shares at a par value of NT$10 per share.</p>
<p>The acquisition of additional shares, payable in cash, would raise Transpac's stake to 15.38 percent of UMM's equity or 46.15 million shares.</p>
<p>Transpac's total share of the investment will be NT$301.40 million, it said.</p>
<p>Other shareholders of UMM include China Rebar Co Ltd, Far Eastern Silo &amp; Shipping Corp and Walsin Lihwa Corp.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
